  "notes": "The prayer over the host, said as the priest raises the paten. Its own document because it accompanies one physical offering and is followed by a change of place at the altar. The demonstrative hic, hæc, hoc carries the plain lemma key hic — SCHEMA.md gives the bare key to the word a reader is likelier to look up — while the adverb lives under hic_adverbium (so at ordinarium.aufer-a-nobis w031). Discriminated keys map back through LEMMA_ALIASES, and the analyzers vote on both. NEGLIGÉNTIIS at w028 is the reading of the printed 1962 books and of witness handmissal-eo; witness do sets the classical spelling neglegéntiis, adjudicated in the apparatus as an orthographic variant. MEIS at w029 carries no gender: the possessive covers three nouns of two genders (peccátis neuter, offensiónibus and negligéntiis feminine), the form marks none, and nothing else settles it. ÓMNIBUS at w032 and w037 is tagged masculine on the substantives it stands with, not on its own form. DEFÚNCTIS at w042 is tagged as the adjective defunctus rather than as a participle of defungor: it stands paired with vivis, an adjective, and both analyzers read the form under an adjectival head — the corpus already treats benedictus the same way. ILLIS at w046 is dative plural masculine by the sense of the sentence: the form marks neither the case against the ablative nor the gender.",
